        <p>Wine also comes 12 bottles to a case, which is 60 glasses. Spirits in 1.75 L bottles are the most economical way to buy for a crowd, but 750s are easier to spread across a bar.</p>

        <h2>The Party Calculator: 4 Hours, Beer/Wine/Spirits Bar</h2>
        <p>This assumes a full bar where guests split roughly 40% beer, 40% wine, and 20% cocktails, at 5 drinks per guest. Shift the columns to match your crowd; a beer-and-wine-only party just moves the spirits share into the other two.</p>
        <table class="guide-table">
