        <h2>Wedding-Specific Tips</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Count the toast separately.</strong> One 750 ml bottle of sparkling wine pours about 6 toast-sized glasses, so figure one bottle per 6 guests for the toast, on top of the table above.</li>
          <li><strong>Cocktail hour drinks faster.</strong> Plan 2 drinks per guest for that first hour even if the reception is mostly beer and wine afterward.</li>
          <li><strong>Signature cocktails simplify everything.</strong> Two signature drinks (say, a ranch water and an Old Fashioned) plus beer and wine keep guests happy and cut your spirits list from six bottles to two kinds.</li>
          <li><strong>Check the venue's rules first.</strong> Many Texas venues that let you bring your own alcohol require a TABC-certified bartender to serve it and don't allow self-service. Ask before you buy.</li>
          <li><strong>Buy a week ahead.</strong> Special orders and big case quantities take a few days to arrive, and you don't want to be doing this the Thursday before.</li>
        </ul>

