        <h2>Party Alcohol FAQ</h2>
        <h3>How much alcohol do I need for 100 guests?</h3>
        <p>For a 4-hour party with a full bar, plan on about 500 drinks: roughly 8 to 9 cases of beer, 40 bottles of wine (about 3 1/2 cases), and 6 to 7 bottles of spirits with about 2 liters of mixer per bottle, plus about 100 pounds of ice.</p>
        <h3>How many bottles of wine for 50 people?</h3>
        <p>If wine is about 40% of what's poured over 4 hours, about 20 bottles. If it's a wine-only event, plan closer to 40 to 50 bottles (about 4 cases), split between white, red, and sparkling to suit the season.</p>
        <h3>How much ice do I need for a party?</h3>
        <p>About 1 pound per guest for a 4-hour indoor party, and up to 2 pounds per guest outdoors in warm weather or if you're icing bottles in tubs. A 20-pound bag covers roughly 15 to 20 guests.</p>
